//
// @PLN153 phase 3 — an INDEX is a slot: `v[j]` and `s[a..b]` with a nullable index read null
// on a null index, and nothing said so.  The corpus census of `convert`'s `τ? ⤳ τ` arm found
// six files doing exactly this after a `find` (which answers `integer?` on a miss, so the
// `if at < 0` guard they carry never fires on the null).  Reported with the rule's split as a
// WARNING at every width, like every seam the phase covers for the first time.
//
// @falsified-at: 806a8d84 → here (warnings 0 → 2): both cells silent on the build this
//   guard was written to catch, same values on both.
//   CHANNEL: the WARNING COUNT — two silent index cells on the control — and nothing else.
//   Falsify has no warning column: a `@EXPECT_WARNING` file gets a direct run where warnings
//   are not matched at all, so both trees read `expect -` and the sweep reports INERT however
//   loudly the diagnostic fires (TESTING.md § A guard that never failed is not a guard,
//   second blind channel).
//   WITNESS: warnings 0 -> 2 on the control against the declared count here; that difference
//   is the whole measurement.
//   HOLDS: the VALUES are identical on both trees, and every channel falsify scores is equal.
//   A run compared on values or exit learns nothing here — count the diagnostics by hand.
// @EXPECT_WARNING: is stored into the index
fn main() {
  i = 0;
  v: vector<integer> = [1, 2, 3];
  j = v[i];                       // integer? — a runtime index
  x = v[j];                       // the vector index
  s = "name=value";
  at = s.find("=");               // integer? — null on a miss
  rest = s[at + 1..];             // the text slice bound
  assert(x == 2, "v[v[0]] is 2: {x}");
  assert(rest == "value", "the slice after `=`: {rest}");
  println("index reported");
}
